      "id": "FA-C438-tahvil-gereftan",
      "sequence": 22420,
      "title": "تحویل گرفتن (tahvil gereftan) — to receive, to take delivery of; to check in (to a room)",
      "headword": "تحویل گرفتن",
      "romanization": "tahvil gereftan",
      "gloss": "to receive, to take delivery of; to check in (to a room)",
      "script": "perso-arabic",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:91ad7bb6c4699d77",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Persian for a suite, then the Persian for to stay."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: تحویل گرفتن",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "تحویل گرفتن (tahvil gereftan) — \"to receive, to take delivery of; to check in (to a room)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ساعت دو اتاق را تحویل گرفتیم. Sâ'at-e do otâq râ tahvil gereftim. We got our room at two o'clock."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The opposite of tahvil dâdan 'to hand over'. Colloquially also to make a fuss of someone."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "tahvil gereftan is built from tahvil 'handing over', a loan usually traced to Arabic taḥwīl 'transfer, turning over' (EtymDB does not list it), and the native verb gereftan 'to take', usually traced to Old Persian grab-."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "tahvil gereftan",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *tahvil gereftan*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "tahvil gereftan, once more",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *tahvil gereftan*, once more]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "a sentence of your own with tahvil gereftan",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: a sentence of your own with *tahvil gereftan*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "RECALL",
              "instruction": "say the Persian for a suite, then the Persian for to stay, then say tahvil gereftan again",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU RECALL: say the Persian for a suite, then the Persian for to stay, then say *tahvil gereftan* again]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 5,
